WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.503 --> 00:00:04.997
- For 20 years, I'd worked
to realize my dream.

00:00:04.997 --> 00:00:06.850
Things don't happen overnight.

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:10.141
If you need to be a
rebel, make sure you win.

00:00:10.141 --> 00:00:11.774
If you're going to be a revolutionary,

00:00:11.774 --> 00:00:13.375
then fight for what you truly believe in.

00:00:13.375 --> 00:00:16.672
Success, what you want to speak about,

00:00:16.672 --> 00:00:18.449
is born out of arrogance.

00:00:18.449 --> 00:00:20.230
People thinkin' they're good.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:23.273
But greatness comes from humility.

00:00:23.273 --> 00:00:25.246
- He's a British chef, restauranteur

00:00:25.246 --> 00:00:26.892
and television personality.

00:00:26.892 --> 00:00:29.369
He has been dubbed, "The
First Celebrity Chef."

00:00:29.369 --> 00:00:31.222
He was, at the time, the youngest chef

00:00:31.222 --> 00:00:33.407
to receive three Michelin stars.

00:00:33.407 --> 00:00:34.759
He's Marco Pierre White.

00:00:34.759 --> 00:00:37.488
And here's my take on his
top 10 rules for success.

00:00:37.488 --> 00:00:39.590
And as always, guys, when
you're watching the videos,

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:41.809
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:41.809 --> 00:00:43.625
please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:00:43.625 --> 00:00:44.458
And put quotes around it,

00:00:44.458 --> 00:00:46.561
so other people can be inspired as well.

00:00:46.561 --> 00:00:48.608
Also, as you are writing something down

00:00:48.608 --> 00:00:51.438
it's much more likely to
stick in your head too.

00:00:51.438 --> 00:00:52.271
Enjoy.

00:01:05.818 --> 00:01:09.044
- My head chef, Robert Reed said to me,

00:01:09.044 --> 00:01:12.471
"So, where do we go from here, Marko?"

00:01:12.471 --> 00:01:14.290
And I said to him,

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:16.522
"When I was a young boy,

00:01:16.522 --> 00:01:19.476
"Mr. Reed used to tell
me abour a restaurant

00:01:19.476 --> 00:01:23.028
"in Paris called La Serre,
which was the ultimate,

00:01:23.028 --> 00:01:24.997
"because it had three stars in Michelin

00:01:24.997 --> 00:01:27.664
"and five red knives and forks."

00:01:29.534 --> 00:01:31.062
I said, "We got three stars

00:01:31.062 --> 00:01:33.812
"and four black knives and forks.

00:01:35.559 --> 00:01:38.919
"Let's go for five red knives and forks."

00:01:38.919 --> 00:01:39.799
For the next three years

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.570
we pushed and we pushed and we pushed

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:43.646
and we did everything.

00:01:43.646 --> 00:01:44.896
In January '98,

00:01:46.746 --> 00:01:50.109
we won our three stars with
five red knives and forks.

00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:53.776
I'd realized my dream
all those years later.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:59.754
And that dream I had
when I was 17 years old,

00:01:59.754 --> 00:02:01.671
I was now 37 years old,

00:02:02.585 --> 00:02:07.390
so, for 20 years I'd
worked to realize my dream.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:09.674
Things don't happen overnight.

00:02:09.674 --> 00:02:14.182
You have to make the emotional,
the personal investment

00:02:14.182 --> 00:02:15.990
to make your dreams come true.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:20.157
Many people have condemned
me for being controversial.

00:02:22.276 --> 00:02:24.752
I was never controversial.

00:02:24.752 --> 00:02:28.252
As I've always said, most of my reputation

00:02:29.205 --> 00:02:32.728
is the product of
exaggeration and ignorance.

00:02:32.728 --> 00:02:34.199
Did I shout?

00:02:34.199 --> 00:02:35.846
Yes I did.

00:02:35.846 --> 00:02:37.284
But, I led from the front.

00:02:37.284 --> 00:02:38.962
I nailed my colors to the mast.

00:02:38.962 --> 00:02:41.136
I fought for my profession.

00:02:41.136 --> 00:02:44.465
If you're going to be a
rebel, make sure you win.

00:02:44.465 --> 00:02:45.984
If you're going to be a revolutionary,

00:02:45.984 --> 00:02:48.110
then fight for what you truly believe in.

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:50.360
And that's all I ever did.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.637
And the boys behind me, they followed me.

00:02:52.637 --> 00:02:57.201
My father sent me to Harrogate,
which was a spa town,

00:02:57.201 --> 00:02:59.229
and told me to find a job.

00:02:59.229 --> 00:03:01.997
The most daunting task in my life.

00:03:01.997 --> 00:03:04.363
And I went to Harrogate and I found a job

00:03:04.363 --> 00:03:06.893
at the Hotel St. George in Harrogate.

00:03:06.893 --> 00:03:11.154
And I started there on
the 20th of March, 1978.

00:03:11.154 --> 00:03:12.719
It wasn't great food,

00:03:12.719 --> 00:03:15.961
but what they taught me was how to push,

00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:18.711
how to run, how to be consistent,

00:03:19.874 --> 00:03:22.969
because consistency is
born out of discipline.

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:24.567
How never to be late.

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:27.054
How to go to work when
you're not feeling well

00:03:27.054 --> 00:03:29.086
and let the chef send you home.

00:03:29.086 --> 00:03:31.419
Success is born out of luck.

00:03:32.831 --> 00:03:33.911
It's an awareness of mind

00:03:33.911 --> 00:03:37.706
that takes advantage of that opportunity.

00:03:37.706 --> 00:03:41.121
You'll all be confronted with opportunity.

00:03:41.121 --> 00:03:43.636
You must take advantage of it,

00:03:43.636 --> 00:03:45.735
because, if you don't take
advantage of your opportunity,

00:03:45.735 --> 00:03:48.067
you'll never realize your dreams.

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:50.563
Whether you want them
or not is irrelevance.

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:53.474
You don't know that until you achieve it.

00:03:53.474 --> 00:03:56.891
I think what gave me the drive to succeed

00:03:58.382 --> 00:04:00.049
was my insecurities.

00:04:01.155 --> 00:04:03.572
Reading, writing, struggling.

00:04:04.631 --> 00:04:07.629
It gave me that individual
drive to prove myself,

00:04:07.629 --> 00:04:10.297
because I'd been belittled at school.

00:04:10.297 --> 00:04:12.192
I've never been taken serious.

00:04:12.192 --> 00:04:16.500
I was always looked upon as
being a fool, as being stupid.

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:19.000
So, it was the fuel behind me,

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:22.641
and that's what made me work far harder,

00:04:22.641 --> 00:04:25.833
was to prove to my father
and other individuals,

00:04:25.833 --> 00:04:28.009
including several teachers,

00:04:28.009 --> 00:04:30.958
that, you know, maybe I struggled
with reading and writing,

00:04:30.958 --> 00:04:34.490
but I had and possess
other great qualities.

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:36.498
So, had I been dealt with as a child,

00:04:36.498 --> 00:04:39.104
I may never had the energy or the fuel

00:04:39.104 --> 00:04:41.820
to drive me to get to where I got.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:44.799
I'm not a celebrity, I'm not a talent,

00:04:44.799 --> 00:04:48.117
I'm no one special, I'm like
everyone else in this world.

00:04:48.117 --> 00:04:51.043
What I crave is ordinary,
which I said to you earlier,

00:04:51.043 --> 00:04:52.941
is I come to work and I do my job,

00:04:52.941 --> 00:04:55.743
and my job today, really, if I'm honest,

00:04:55.743 --> 00:04:59.910
is inspiring the young, like
having the catering students

00:05:00.852 --> 00:05:02.656
come and visit me this afternoon

00:05:02.656 --> 00:05:05.258
and show me respect and kindness.

00:05:05.258 --> 00:05:08.489
And I only hope that my
stories and my philosophies

00:05:08.489 --> 00:05:10.987
and my thoughts inspire them.

00:05:10.987 --> 00:05:13.904
The last thing I said to them today

00:05:15.341 --> 00:05:19.042
is a story is more
important than a recipe.

00:05:19.042 --> 00:05:23.606
A recipe can confuse you,
but a story can inspire you.

00:05:23.606 --> 00:05:25.333
When I was a young boy,

00:05:25.333 --> 00:05:26.892
I had that privilege
of working with people

00:05:26.892 --> 00:05:28.838
like the great Michael
Lawson at The Box Tree.

00:05:28.838 --> 00:05:31.477
The great owners of The Box
Tree, Mr. Reed and Mr. Long.

00:05:31.477 --> 00:05:33.150
Ken Lamb the baker.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:36.817
Albert Pierre Kalfon,
the great Ramon Balan.

00:05:38.017 --> 00:05:40.781
What did they really teach me?

00:05:40.781 --> 00:05:42.331
Was how to tell stories.

00:05:42.331 --> 00:05:44.659
How to inspire people.

00:05:44.659 --> 00:05:46.126
That's what's important.

00:05:46.126 --> 00:05:48.975
I've had lots of bad luck in my life.

00:05:48.975 --> 00:05:53.323
But, I think having bad luck
is equally as important.

00:05:53.323 --> 00:05:55.385
Because, when you have bad luck in life,

00:05:55.385 --> 00:05:56.963
you have to reflect,

00:05:56.963 --> 00:06:00.398
you have to take the knowledge
from that experience.

00:06:00.398 --> 00:06:02.041
We've all been treated badly.

00:06:02.041 --> 00:06:04.438
We've all made mistakes.

00:06:04.438 --> 00:06:06.011
We've all had bad luck.

00:06:06.011 --> 00:06:08.303
So, what we have to do is reflect,

00:06:08.303 --> 00:06:09.820
take the knowledge from the experience,

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:12.440
and then allow it to enrich our life.

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:13.862
It's as simple as that.

00:06:13.862 --> 00:06:15.035
And, let's be honest,

00:06:15.035 --> 00:06:18.928
when people do you have any
regrets Marco, I say, "No."

00:06:18.928 --> 00:06:22.090
Because had it not been for
all those mistakes I made

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:24.738
I wouldn't have the
knowledge that I have today,

00:06:24.738 --> 00:06:26.807
I wouldn't have the
experience that I have today,

00:06:26.807 --> 00:06:28.890
because mistakes are fine

00:06:29.794 --> 00:06:32.599
as long as you take the
knowledge from the mistake.

00:06:32.599 --> 00:06:34.473
And, so, the one thing my father gave me,

00:06:34.473 --> 00:06:37.610
which is really key, was that work ethic.

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:39.347
That ability to get
myself up in the morning

00:06:39.347 --> 00:06:41.750
no matter how tired I was

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:44.090
to push myself through
those pain barriers.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:48.257
And, again, the combination
of the loss of a mother at six

00:06:49.928 --> 00:06:52.763
and, then, being sent out to work at 10,

00:06:52.763 --> 00:06:54.572
I mean, started work at
five o'clock in the morning

00:06:54.572 --> 00:06:55.592
through the milk round,

00:06:55.592 --> 00:06:58.461
being dropped off at 8:45
at school in the milk van,

00:06:58.461 --> 00:07:00.209
you know, that work ethic,

00:07:00.209 --> 00:07:03.264
so, that combination of those two,

00:07:03.264 --> 00:07:05.978
work ethic and great insecurity

00:07:05.978 --> 00:07:08.138
was what got me to where I went to.

00:07:08.138 --> 00:07:10.352
I turned my dream into reality.

00:07:10.352 --> 00:07:13.671
But, sometimes reality is
not what you think it is.

00:07:13.671 --> 00:07:14.744
Winning three stars

00:07:14.744 --> 00:07:17.828
was the most exciting journey of my life.

00:07:17.828 --> 00:07:21.016
Then, the day comes where
you're king of your world.

00:07:21.016 --> 00:07:23.496
And people views of you now change,

00:07:23.496 --> 00:07:26.282
because you're up there,

00:07:26.282 --> 00:07:28.550
and you have to play a systematic game.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:29.971
It's a formula.

00:07:29.971 --> 00:07:33.263
You just roll out the same
dishes day in, day out.

00:07:33.263 --> 00:07:35.145
And then, you know,

00:07:35.145 --> 00:07:37.642
I sat down one day and thought to myself,

00:07:37.642 --> 00:07:40.339
"Do I really want to do this anymore?

00:07:40.339 --> 00:07:42.493
It's not pleasurable."

00:07:42.493 --> 00:07:45.608
And, so, I sat down and
I thought to myself,

00:07:45.608 --> 00:07:47.086
"What are my options?"

00:07:47.086 --> 00:07:51.253
My first option was to continue
working six days a week,

00:07:52.288 --> 00:07:54.104
between 80 and 100 hours a week.

00:07:54.104 --> 00:07:56.521
My second option, live a lie.

00:07:57.647 --> 00:08:00.024
Pretend I cook when I don't cook.

00:08:00.024 --> 00:08:03.693
My third option was to pluck
up the courage from within,

00:08:03.693 --> 00:08:06.253
to give back my stars,

00:08:06.253 --> 00:08:08.670
to abdicate from my position,

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:14.237
to accept that tomorrow I'm
unemployed, I have no status.

00:08:15.998 --> 00:08:17.665
But, what do I have?

00:08:18.795 --> 00:08:22.856
I have an opportunity to
discover myself as a person

00:08:22.856 --> 00:08:24.963
and to let go of everything
that I've ever worked for,

00:08:24.963 --> 00:08:26.651
to let go of my status,

00:08:26.651 --> 00:08:31.475
to walk away from my dream
is a very tough decision.

00:08:31.475 --> 00:08:35.937
And, one day, a little thought
just drifted into my mind.

00:08:35.937 --> 00:08:38.793
And that little thought was

00:08:38.793 --> 00:08:40.249
that I am being judged

00:08:40.249 --> 00:08:43.749
by people who have less knowledge than me.

00:08:44.614 --> 00:08:46.527
So, what is it all worth?

00:08:46.527 --> 00:08:47.527
Very little.

00:08:49.221 --> 00:08:53.388
And, so, that's what gave
me the courage to walk away.

00:08:54.802 --> 00:08:57.161
You have to fight the ego every day.

00:08:57.161 --> 00:09:00.911
The ego is the most
extraordinary part of us,

00:09:02.859 --> 00:09:04.494
because, when we think we've suppressed it

00:09:04.494 --> 00:09:06.235
and we've beaten it,

00:09:06.235 --> 00:09:08.820
it manifests itself into
another form and another shape

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:10.388
and starts to take you over again.

00:09:10.388 --> 00:09:13.248
And, so, every day you
have to fight the ego

00:09:13.248 --> 00:09:17.662
and allow the humility to
come through, in my opinion,

00:09:17.662 --> 00:09:20.744
and, by allowing humility to come through,

00:09:20.744 --> 00:09:22.494
because, let's be honest,

00:09:22.494 --> 00:09:25.712
success, which you want to speak about,

00:09:25.712 --> 00:09:27.443
is born out of arrogance.

00:09:27.443 --> 00:09:29.384
People thinkin' they're good.

00:09:29.384 --> 00:09:32.983
But, greatness comes from humility.

00:09:32.983 --> 00:09:35.658
And, being successful is not good enough.

00:09:35.658 --> 00:09:39.259
It's all about being great
at whatever we go in life.

00:09:39.259 --> 00:09:41.401
You can have the most
humble job in the world,

00:09:41.401 --> 00:09:44.336
but you can be truly great.

00:09:44.336 --> 00:09:48.083
You can be a humble guy, but
you can be a great person.

00:09:48.083 --> 00:09:49.554
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:09:49.554 --> 00:09:52.385
I made this video because
Ian Atkins asked me to.

00:09:52.385 --> 00:09:53.437
So, if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:09:53.437 --> 00:09:55.110
that you want me to profile next,

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:56.443
leave it down in the comments below

00:09:56.443 --> 00:09:57.556
and I'll see what I can do.

00:09:57.556 --> 00:09:59.009
I'd also love to know what did Marco say

00:09:59.009 --> 00:10:01.232
that had the biggest
impact on you and why.

00:10:01.232 --> 00:10:02.500
What did you learn from this video

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:05.447
that you're going to
immediately apply to your life

00:10:05.447 --> 00:10:06.570
or to your business?

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:08.543
Leave it in the comments
and I'll see what I can do.

00:10:08.543 --> 00:10:09.716
Finally, I want to give a quick shout out

00:10:09.716 --> 00:10:11.643
to Anastasia Zinchenko,

00:10:11.643 --> 00:10:13.882
thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:10:13.882 --> 00:10:14.718
Your One Word,

00:10:14.718 --> 00:10:17.817
and making that awesome
YouTube video on it as well.

00:10:17.817 --> 00:10:20.076
I really, really, really
appreciate your support.

00:10:20.076 --> 00:10:22.848
- Believe in yourself,
believe in your abilities,

00:10:22.848 --> 00:10:25.583
and believe in your future.

00:10:25.583 --> 00:10:26.964
- So, thank you guys again for watching.

00:10:26.964 --> 00:10:28.037
I believe in you.

00:10:28.037 --> 00:10:30.174
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:10:30.174 --> 00:10:32.262
and whatever your one word is.

00:10:32.262 --> 00:10:34.679
Much love, I'll see you soon.

